 Thamel and Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ole Miss sues LSU's Umanmielen, Harper for breach of contract","description":"Ole Miss is seeking close to $1 million in penalties from former players Princewill Umanmielen and Devin Harper, who signed revenue sharing contracts to return to the Rebels this season before joining former coach Lane Kiffin at LSU.","published":"2026-07-29T12:13:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49475144/ole-miss-sues-former-players-princewill-umanmielen-devin-harper-now-lsu-breach-contract","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wyoming's Jay Sawvel gets self-imposed 1-game ban over tampering violations","description":"Wyoming head coach Jay Sawvel will serve a one-game suspension Saturday as part of the school's self-imposed penalties for impermissible contacts to players.","published":"2026-11-24T23:34:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586972/wyoming-coach-jay-sawvel-gets-self-imposed-1-game-suspension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 20 Florida shuts down WR Vernell Brown for season-ending knee surgery","description":"No. 20 Florida is shutting down receiver Vernell Brown III for the remainder of the season.","published":"2026-11-24T23:07:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586755/no-20-florida-shuts-wr-vernell-brown-season-ending-knee-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Viral couple from Wake Forest-Georgia Tech game speaks on 'Today' show","description":"The couple's intense discussion was caught on an ESPN broadcast of Wake Forest and Georgia Tech's Week 12 game and went viral.","published":"2026-11-24T21:02:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584732/wake-forest-georgia-tech-viral-couple-speaks","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado's Deion Sanders shrugs off hot-seat chatter before UCF","description":"Deion Sanders handles outside chatter -- in this case, speculation over his future as coach at Colorado -- by simply tuning out the noise.","published":"2026-11-24T21:29:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585728/colorado-sanders-shrugs-hot-seat-chatter-ucf","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Memphis' Charles Huff says he's not candidate for Maryland head coaching job","description":"Memphis' Charles Huff said he's not a candidate for the head coaching vacancy at Maryland and will not be part of this year's coaching carousel.","published":"2026-11-24T20:33:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585465/charles-huff-says-not-candidate-maryland-hc-job","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NCAA sanctions Liberty over tampering with two players before entering portal","description":"Among the penalties the NCAA announced against Liberty, two coaches and the GM received show-cause penalties over tampering.","published":"2026-11-24T20:05:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585093/ncaa-sanctions-liberty-transfer-portal-tampering","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star OT Lincoln Fa'alafi commits to Notre Dame, to join 2028 class","description":"New Zealand native Lincoln Fa'alafi, ESPN's No. 8 overall prospect in the 2028 cycle, committed Tuesday to Notre Dame.","published":"2026-11-24T19:56:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584881/notre-dame-gets-2028-commitment-ot-lincoln-faalafi","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"A timeline of Michigan athletics since 2017","description":"Warde Manuel's eventful decade in Ann Arbor has been marked by athletic successes and marred by controversy.","published":"2026-11-24T18:47:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49351177/2026-michigan-warde-manuel-athletic-department-tenure-line-investigation","type":"Story","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4917971/princewill-umanmielen","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princewill_Umanmielen"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Princewill Umanmielen","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princewill_Umanmielen","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:45Z","intro":"Princewill Umanmielen (born February 13, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the LSU Tigers. He previously played for the Nebraska Cornhuskers and Ole Miss Rebels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Umanmielen attended Manor High School in Manor, Texas. In his final two seasons, he totaled 47 tackles for loss and 21 sacks. A four-star recruit, Umanmielen committed to play college football at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln over offers from Arkansas, Florida, and Washington."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"NEBRASKA\nAs a freshman, Umanmielen recorded 22 tackles, 4.5 tackles-for-loss, and a sack. As a result, he was named a second-team freshman All-American. The following season, he tallied 13 tackles and 2.5 tackles-for-loss, before entering the transfer portal.\n\nOLE MISS\nOn December 14, 2024, Umanmielen, a top-ranked transfer, announced his decision to transfer to the University of Mississippi to play for the Ole Miss Rebels."}],"family":[{"relation":"Sibling","name":"Princely Umanmielen","description":"American football defensive end (born 2002)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princely_Umanmielen"}]}}